. The state's partisan lean favors Republicans by about five points, and Donalds has built a large financial edge, raising nearly $14 million with backing from most of the billionaires active in the race. Jolly, a former Republican congressman running as a Democrat, has pressed national party leaders for funds.\n\nMost race raters call Florida Lean Republican, with one rating it Solid R and one a Tossup. Averages of published polls put Donalds ahead by roughly two to six points, and prediction markets give Jolly about a one-in-four chance. Headlines describe the race as surprisingly close, and a data-center controversy has tested Donalds, but the weight of the evidence still favors the Republican in this open-seat contest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1709, "margin": -5.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2654, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2923, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2636, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1983, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2414, "margin": -3.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2597, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2217, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2584, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.252, "margin": -4.3}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2745, "margin": -3.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2552, "margin": -4.2}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2498, "margin": -4.2}]}